/*!
    \page index.html
    \inmodule CodeLanguages
    \title Code Languages

    Code is marked up as C++ by default:
    \code
    // Some C++ code:
    QWidget *widget = getWidget();
    \endcode

    Code can be explicitly marked up as C++ with the \c Cpp language:
    \code [Cpp]
    // Some C++ code:
    QWidget *widget = getWidget();
    \endcode

    QML code can be requested with the \c QML language:
    \code [QML]
    // Some QML code:
    Item {
        id: my_item
    }
    \endcode

    Plain text is shown if the \c text language is used:
    \code [text]
    // Some C++ code:
    QWidget *widget = getWidget();

    // Some QML code:
    Item {
        id: my_item
    }
    \endcode

    The case of the specified language is not important:
    \code [CPP]
    // Some C++ code:
    QWidget *widget = getWidget();
    \endcode

    Languages that QDoc does not handle are accepted but not processed
    if the language was declared in the \c languages configuration
    variable:
    \code [Python]
    def fn():
        pass
    \endcode

    A warning will be generated if the language is unknown and not listed
    in the \c languages configuration variable:
    \code [BASIC]
    10 PRINT "Hello world!"
    20 GOTO 10
    \endcode
*/
